Automation alert-resolution outcomes
====================================

The alert.resolve action uses the rule's trusted organization context. Action
parameters cannot override that context. Missing, foreign or unavailable alerts
and a service refusal are failed actions; execution history records failure and
the next action runs only if continue_on_error is enabled. The existing resolved
field is retained alongside the standard success field. An already-resolved
alert is a refused change rather than a newly successful resolution.

Internal automated resolution has no interactive user, so resolved_by is NULL.
The system resolution note remains attached to the alert. Do not create a fake
all-zero user to satisfy the foreign key. Interactive API calls still pass their
authenticated user UUID. System resolution events represent absent attribution
as JSON null, not the string "None". No database migration is needed because the
foreign-key column is already nullable.

This correction does not add automatic retries, change authorization or make
alert events transactional with the database commit. The existing event and
notification publication path is not a transactional outbox. Customer delivery,
failover and exactly-once claims still require independent qualification.
